infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Asymmetric strictness: where coercion saves you vs where it lies
  compares
    - label Lax
      children
        - label LAX MODE (the default)
          desc the stringly-typed-web absorber
        - label Coerces along a documented table
          desc digit string to int, true to True, 89.0 passes an int field
        - label Use where strings are structural
          desc query params, headers, env vars, settings
        - label Risk: hides contract drift silently
          desc string money coerced for 5 months, no signal at all
    - label Strict
      children
        - label STRICT MODE (opt-in)
          desc where the type is the contract
        - label Types must match exactly
          desc an int field rejects the string form of a number
        - label Use for money, ids, partner payloads
          desc anything serialized across a boundary
        - label Fails at the first bad payload
          desc one alert, not a peak-time wall of 422s
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
